      "id": "WGR-01",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-weight-one-crystalline-steps",
      "title": "Smooth crystalline comparison, natural Hodge–Tate spectral frames, Galois eigenspace realizations, and the step package",
      "statement": "Let ℓ be a prime and E a number field with algebraic closure Ω and Galois group Γ = Gal(Ω/E). (1) For every finite extension K/ℚ_ℓ, the smooth étale comparison side yields a smooth projective Hodge–Tate comparison isomorphism, bijectivity, and natural Hodge–Tate spectral frames Φ_M with ∑_a e_a = d intertwining the étale and Hodge pullback matrices E(u) Φ_M = Φ_(M') H(u) across morphisms u : M' → M of smooth models. (2) Smooth proper integral models have crystalline étale cohomology (B_cris-admissible), establishing both that every Hecke eigenspace piece cut out by an integral smooth cover over O_(E,w) is crystalline at w | ℓ and, paired with universal finite-level crystalline Frobenius annihilation ∑_(i=0)^n (−1)^i ℓ^(f i(i−1)/2) A_i ⊗ φ^(f(n−i+N)) = 0 on invariants, that integral Hecke congruences annihilate crystalline Frobenius at w | ℓ. (3) For every nice Hecke tower H over E and eigenvalue system θ, Galois commutation preserves the simultaneous eigenspace piece, total étale cohomology is finite-dimensional with continuous matrix entries, and Jordan–Hölder semisimplification yields a continuous semisimple representation ρ : Γ → GL_D(Q̄_ℓ) realizing that piece. (4) Combining natural Hodge–Tate frames, crystalline comparison, Čech-cube Hodge base change, trace splitting, and lower-piece correspondence lifts ensures that every complex Hodge weight of a good integral realization at w | ℓ occurs as a filtration jump of ρ|_w. (5) Together with Eichler–Shimura congruence away from ℓ, integral-to-local cut reduction, rank-one twisting, Satake cardinality, jump transfer, richness extraction, and split-line character subtraction, these assemble the complete seventeen-component comparison step package.",
      "hypotheses": "A prime ℓ, a number field E with algebraic closure Ω, finite extensions K/ℚ_ℓ, smooth projective models with finite étale Hecke correspondences, and the smooth étale, Čech-cube, and Eichler–Shimura local comparison inputs established in the preceding sections.",
      "correspondence": "The smooth étale side feeds parallel Hodge–Tate spectral frames and B_cris-admissibility, yielding the crystalline, crystalline-Frobenius, and Hodge–Tate jump steps; Galois-Hecke commutation, finite-dimensional cohomology, continuity, and semisimplification realize every nice Hecke eigenspace as a continuous semisimple representation, assembling all seventeen entries of the comparison step package.",
