    {
      "id": "WGR-02",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-weight-one-kodaira-spencer",
      "title": "Admissible fibre-power towers, good integral models, Galois flag descent, finite-level cohomology descent, and conditional realization",
      "statement": "Let p be a prime and let D, G, L be a PEL unitary datum linked to an algebraic group over ℚ with universal abelian scheme. (1) Whenever an integral Hecke element h satisfies k h^(−1)(Λ̂) ⊆ Λ̂ for a positive integer k, level N k is admissible over level N; translation isogenies compose, pull back, act freely and transitively on level-structure orbits, and descend along finite étale covers, producing smooth fibre powers, nice Hecke towers, and complete Kuga–Sato towers with unique transitive free witness maps. (2) At every prime w where the group-side Hecke test is good, integral lattice generation, finite étale base covers, congruence quotients, and fibre-power extensions yield a smooth integral reduction of the fibre-power Hecke tower. (3) Every finite-dimensional representation admits a Jordan–Hölder flag and change-of-basis matrix P whose conjugate P^(−1) ρ_0 P is block upper triangular with semisimple diagonal-block projection; conjugation invariance and uniqueness of the correspondence characterization force Galois–Hecke commutation (G A G^(−1) = A implies A G = G A); writing an algebraic extension Ω/k as the directed colimit of its finite intermediate extensions L/k expresses X_Ω = lim_L X_L with affine transitions between quasi-compact quasi-separated schemes, so finitariness of torsion Tate twists forces every torsion étale cohomology class to descend to a finite subextension L/k; local base change transports Hecke congruences to crystalline Frobenius data at w | ℓ; and injectivity of integer casting transfers highest-weight jumps to Hodge–Tate jump occurrence. (4) Combining the step package, the six-part Kuga–Sato package, and automorphic plan existence yields the weight-one geometric realization conditional only on the holomorphic Lefschetz trace formula.",
      "hypotheses": "A prime p, a PEL unitary Shimura datum with universal abelian family, a Hecke tower over a CM number field E, an algebraic extension Ω/k, a quasi-compact quasi-separated scheme X over k, and the seventeen-component comparison step package of WGR-01.",
      "correspondence": "Admissible congruence levels, translation isogeny descent, and integral reduction supply smooth nice fibre-power towers with good integral models; Jordan–Hölder flag conjugation, uniqueness-forced Galois commutation, directed-colimit descent of torsion étale cohomology, local crystalline transport, and integer-jump recovery connect them to the step package, assembling weight-one geometric realization modulo the holomorphic Lefschetz formula.",
