      "id": "WGR-03",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-weight-one-geo-assembly",
      "title": "Clopen holomorphic Lefschetz reduction and unconditional weight-one geometric realizations",
      "statement": "Let Z be a smooth projective scheme over ℂ of pure relative dimension d (not assumed connected), and let c_1, c_2 : Y → Z be finite étale morphisms over ℂ whose complex fixed-point locus F = {y ∈ Y(ℂ) : c_1(y) = c_2(y)} is finite and transverse, meaning that the local tangent matrix A_y ∈ M_d(ℂ) of c_2 ∘ c_1^(−1) at each y ∈ F satisfies det(I_d − A_y) ≠ 0. (1) Quasi-compactness and smoothness decompose Z into finitely many pairwise disjoint integral clopen projective components Z = ⊔_(j ∈ J) V_j, pulling back to a clopen cover W_(j,k) = c_1^(−1)(V_j) ∩ c_2^(−1)(V_k) of Y with finite étale restrictions c_(1,j,k) : W_(j,k) → V_j and c_(2,j,k) : W_(j,k) → V_k. (2) Open restriction gives an isomorphism H^b(Z, Ω^a) ≅ ∏_(j ∈ J) H^b(V_j, Ω^a) identifying c_(1*) c_2^* with the block matrix (T_(j,k)) whose off-diagonal blocks (j ≠ k) drop out of the trace, yielding finite dimensionality of H^b(Z, Ω^a) and tr(c_(1*) c_2^*) = ∑_(j ∈ J) tr(T_(j,j)). (3) Every fixed point y ∈ F satisfies c_1(y) = c_2(y) ∈ V_j for a unique j ∈ J, lifts uniquely into the diagonal clopen piece W_(j,j) with unchanged tangent matrix A_y, and applying the integral-component holomorphic Lefschetz formula on each (V_j, W_(j,j)) yields ∑_(b=0)^d (−1)^b tr(c_(1*) c_2^* | H^b(Z, Ω^a)) = ∑_(y ∈ F) [t^a] det(I_d + t A_y) / det(I_d − A_y) for every integer a ≥ 0. (4) Exporting this formula discharges the sole remaining holomorphic Lefschetz hypothesis of WGR-02 and delivers the unconditional weight-one geometric realization theorem: for any odd rank m, CM field E, prime ℓ, separated places w_0, v' | ℓ with lacunary weight at v', and auxiliary automorphic representation U, there exist continuous semisimple Galois realizations realizing the base comparison, Eichler–Shimura Satake annihilation at every eligible spherical prime w ∤ ℓ, and both crystalline Hodge–Tate jump occurrence and crystalline Frobenius Satake annihilation at every separated auxiliary prime w | ℓ.",
      "hypotheses": "A smooth projective complex scheme Z of pure relative dimension d, a finite étale correspondence c_1, c_2 : Y → Z over ℂ with finite transverse complex fixed-point locus F, the irreducible-component holomorphic Lefschetz formula, and the conditional weight-one geometric realization assembly of WGR-01 and WGR-02.",
      "correspondence": "Disjoint clopen integral decomposition turns global Hodge cohomology into a finite product whose correspondence trace depends solely on diagonal blocks W_(j,j), while every fixed point lands uniquely in a diagonal block; summing the irreducible holomorphic Lefschetz formula across components exports the general trace identity and closes the unconditional weight-one geometric realization.",
